\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Sensitivity of the Bard experiment to $\delta $ and $\sigma _{\min }$. The values of $f(x^*)$ and the drop factor between $o=3$ and $o=4$ are those of the first-order method; the second-order variant agrees with them to within the multistart variability. The count columns give the mean \#it and \#fcnt over the $100$ starting points, summed over $o=1,\dots  ,6$. In all $24$ runs the $o=4$ solution identified exactly the four added outliers.}}{16}{table.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:sens}{{4}{16}{Sensitivity of the Bard experiment to $\delta $ and $\sigma _{\min }$. The values of $f(x^*)$ and the drop factor between $o=3$ and $o=4$ are those of the first-order method; the second-order variant agrees with them to within the multistart variability. The count columns give the mean \#it and \#fcnt over the $100$ starting points, summed over $o=1,\dots ,6$. In all $24$ runs the $o=4$ solution identified exactly the four added outliers}{table.4}{}}
